    goals: "Eradicate infection, reduce contagion, prevent complications (corneal involvement, recurrent infections)",
    pharm: "1. Topical antibiotic (first-line): Chloramphenicol 0.5% eye drops — 1-2 drops q2h for 2 days, then q4h for 5-7 days. OR Fusidic Acid 1% gel — BID for 7 days (less frequent, cream-based — good for children). 2. Alternative (if allergy or MRSA): Ciprofloxacin 0.3% or Ofloxacin 0.3% eye drops q2-6h. 3. Cleaning: Gently cleanse eyelids with sterile saline or clean water. 4. No role for systemic antibiotics in simple conjunctivitis.",
